**V61-D2 (P1).** The one §4.4 minimum-safe member missing from `MINIMUM_SAFE_CONTEXT` is *"exact canonical entity and action state for the targets of this turn"*. The named-this-turn rows live only inside `companies`/`people`/`tasks`/`goals`, all four `TRIM_ORDER` keys, and the second hard pass uses floor **0**. Measured, with one heavy newest history row and 400-char free text elsewhere: `companies` and `people` → 0 rows, `QA-VERIFY-NAMED-CO` and `QA-VERIFY-NAMED-PERSON` gone, **and the turn still ships at 10,868 tokens**. The founder gets an answer built on a pack in which the company they just named is absent. Company/task/goal archive-restore survive (server-side resolution); rename, assign, set-manager, create-under-parent and every read about that entity do not.

